# Notes record edge cases and complexity; the coverage summary counts them.
:inputs nums

say Return the largest number.
add root:
    best = nums[0]
    for num~loopvar in nums:
        if num > best:
            best = num
    return best
:coverage

say If the list is empty there's no answer; that's an edge case.
note n2 edge-case: An empty list has no largest number.

say It's one pass, so linear time.
note root complexity: O(n) time, O(1) space.
note n7: Could use max(), but this shows the loop.
show
:coverage

say Scratch the remark about max.
unnote n23
expect gaps none
:coverage
